iew which is  a digital series i do to pick the minds  of  you know uh people that i admire  especially in the journalistic  sense curious people people who have  figured out how to have  an art in the interview itself  what is something that  is advice i'm asking for myself here  what is advice to asking that surprising  question that might catch off guard  might be a bit  pushy but really is going to ultimately  bring  insight into that person we're not  getting otherwise  i think it starts with trust and i think  you're really good at that  actually which is that you are open  yourself  you're willing to share which you've  been on our show twice by the way  and it's a short list of the sun it's  you dolly eine garten there's like four  people and you're  you're in that company my goodness but  you i know  if i can build trust with you and you  know that number one i've  i'm well researched that i'm not  interested in whatever the gotcha  question  is from the gossip magazine that's just  not what i do  if you can start a conversation and  frankly on our show we have time you  know i sit with somebody as you know for  45 minutes or an hour  so even if i don't know the person i'm  building a rapport so once you have that  trust  you you might not even have to ask the  question they might just start sharing  something with you or talking about  you know i don't like to zero in on pain  in someone's life  but if i feel like we've got enough of a  relationship in the interview that  they're willing to go there  then i will or a lot of times as i say  it will just come out because we've  built that rapport over the course of  the interview  i definitely am someone who is  willing to go there myself and i would  like to  welcome um anyone else to go there with  me and  what you just said made me think of your  signature piece in your show the highs  and the lows  and i was wondering if i could turn that  question on to you  i love that and why don't we start with  the 